# Build artifacts of the standalone plugin (its own workspace target/) and the
# grammar checkout its build.rs makes. The grammar is deliberately NOT
# vendored — see README.md.
/target
/grammar-src
# WT.2: written by build.rs from the `lattice-wit` dependency. Vendoring it is
# what let it drift behind the editor's ABI.
/wit
# The integration package is its own workspace, so it has its own target/.
# `/target` above is root-anchored and does not reach it.
/integration/target
# Written by the CI test step so one run can be asserted twice.
/integration/test.log
# The integration package's lock pins LATTICE's dependency graph (its path
# dependencies are the editor's own crates), so committed it went stale on
# every lattice dependency change and sat in `git status` as churn org does
# not own. It is seeded from lattice's own lock instead: in CI by the test
# job, on a fresh clone by hand (README, "The integration suite").
/integration/Cargo.lock
